====Hybe Japan====
{{Anchor|Hybe Japan}}
Following Hybe's second leadership restructuring in July 2021, its Japanese subsidiaries, Hybe Solutions Japan and Hybe T&D Japan,{{Efn|formerly TNDJ}} were integrated to form a regional headquarters, Hybe Japan. The Japanese branch operates as an independent entity under CEO and former Hybe Solutions Japan CEO Hyunrock Han.<ref>{{cite web|title=HYBE CEO steps down to focus on music production|url=https://www.kedglobal.com/newsView/ked202107020004|work=[[The Korea Economic Daily]]|last=Seong|first=Soo-young|date=July 2, 2021|access-date=August 15, 2021|archive-date=July 2, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210702071954/https://www.kedglobal.com/newsView/ked202107020004|url-status=live}}</ref> It oversees music production, music publishing, music copyright management, artist management, and talent scouting and development,<ref name="HybeJapan">{{cite news|title=Inside Hybe: Seven agencies making a splash on the music scene|url=http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20210715001079|newspaper=[[The Korea Herald]]|last=Park|first=Jun-hee|date=July 19, 2021|access-date=August 15, 2021|archive-date=July 20, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210720063436/http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20210715001079|url-status=live}}</ref> as well as facilitates the entry of other Hybe artists into the Japanese market.<ref name="Bang resigns CEO" /> Hybe Labels Japan debuted its first boy group, [[&Team]], in December 2022.<ref>{{cite news|title=Hybe's first Japanese band &Team makes global debut|url=https://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20221207000615|newspaper=[[The Korea Herald]]|last=Choi|first=Ji-won|date=December 7, 2022|access-date=July 13, 2023|archive-date=December 7, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221207065721/https://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20221207000615|url-status=live}}</ref> A collaboration with [[Hiroomi Tosaka]] of [[Sandaime J Soul Brothers|J Soul Brothers]], announced in 2021,<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:EXILE・三代目JSBら所属のLDH、男女混合の大型オーディション詳細発表 BTSら輩出・HYBEとの共同プロデュースも＜iCON Z ～Dreams For Children＞ - モデルプレス|url=https://mdpr.jp/news/detail/2674584|website=ModelPress|language=ja|date=July 16, 2021|access-date=August 15, 2021|archive-date=July 15, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210715194706/https://mdpr.jp/news/detail/2674584|url-status=live}}</ref> resulted in the creation of the girl group [[Moonchild (group)|Moonchild]], which debuted in 2023;<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:LDH新グループ・MOONCHILDが初パフォーマンス進化を止めずに進んでいきます|trans-title=|url=https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2278308/full/|work=Oricon Music|language=ja|date=May 9, 2023|access-date=July 13, 2023|archive-date=May 22, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230522054930/https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2278308/full/|url-status=live}}</ref> Hybe Labels Japan co-produces the group with [[LDH (company)|LDH Japan]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:LDH 5人組ガールズグループMOONCHILD5・3デビュー OMI(登坂広臣)プロデュース、HYBE LABELS JAPAN制作|trans-title=LDH's five-member girl group "MOONCHILD" debuts on May 3rd, produced by OMI (Hiroomi Tosaka) and Hybe Labels Japan|url=https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2269397/full/|work=Oricon Music|language=ja|date=February 27, 2023|access-date=July 13, 2023|archive-date=February 27, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230227224539/https://www.oricon.co.jp/news/2269397/full/|url-status=live}}</ref> Moonchild's music is produced by ØMI, with production handled by ALYSA, a producer and composer from Hybe Labels Japan. LDH Japan handles the management of the group.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:LDHオーディション「iCON Z」発のガールズグループ・MOONCHILDが5月にデビュー|trans-title=MOONCHILD, the girl group born from LDH's audition show 'iCON Z,' is set to debut in May.|url=https://natalie.mu/music/news/514444|work=natalie|language=ja|date=February 26, 2023|access-date=May 18, 2026}}</ref> In 2025, Hybe Labels Japan rebranded as YX Labels.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE rebrands Japan-headquartered division as YX LABELS|url=https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/hybe-rebrands-japan-headquartered-division-as-yx-labels/|website=Music Business Worldwide|last=Stassen|first=Murray|date=February 17, 2025|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=February 17, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217194007/https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/hybe-rebrands-japan-headquartered-division-as-yx-labels/|url-status=live}}</ref> In March 12, 2025, Naeco officially registered its closure and ceased operations.<ref>{{Cite web |script-title=ja: 国税庁法人番号公表サイト 株式会社NAECOの情報|trans-title=National Tax Agency Corporate Number Publication Site: Information on NAECO Co., Ltd.|url=https://www.houjin-bangou.nta.go.jp/henkorireki-johoto.html?selHouzinNo=7010401171358 |website=houjin-bangou |access-date=May 18, 2026}}</ref> In January 2026, Hybe Japan launched a new label, Jconic.<ref name=":6" /> 

