====Hybe Latin America====
{{Anchor|Hybe Lartin America}}
In November 2023, Hybe announced the creation of its [[Latin music]] division, '''Hybe Latin America''', with offices in [[Mexico City]], [[Los Angeles]], and [[Miami]]. J.H. Kah, former vice president of [[YG Entertainment]], was appointed as [[Chief executive officer|CEO]], after the company confirmed the acquisition of Exile Content.<ref>{{cite web|title=K-pop giant Hybe buys its first Latin music company|url=https://www.straitstimes.com/life/entertainment/k-pop-giant-hybe-buys-its-first-latin-music-company|website=The Straits Times|date=November 13, 2023|access-date=November 13, 2023|archive-date=November 13, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231113110024/https://www.straitstimes.com/life/entertainment/k-pop-giant-hybe-buys-its-first-latin-music-company|url-status=live}}</ref> In March 2024, Fernando Grediaga, previously an executive at EMI-[[Universal Music México]], became general manager of Hybe Latin America.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE, firma coreana que maneja a BTS abre oficina en México|url=https://www.elsoldemexico.com.mx/gossip/hybe-firma-coreana-que-maneja-a-bts-abre-oficina-en-mexico-11570577.html|website=El Sol de México {{!}} Noticias, Deportes, Gossip, Columnas|language=es|last=México|first=Úrsula Medina / El Sol de|access-date=March 10, 2024|archive-date=March 10, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240310052609/https://www.elsoldemexico.com.mx/gossip/hybe-firma-coreana-que-maneja-a-bts-abre-oficina-en-mexico-11570577.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The leadership team also includes [[Isaac Lee]] as chairman and Juan S. Arenas as [[Chief operating officer|COO]].<ref name="Garcia">{{Cite web|title=HYBE Latin America Eyes Growth With Reality TV Push, Interactive Exhibits, and New Deals with Daddy Yankee and Morat|url=https://variety.com/2025/music/news/hybe-latin-america-reality-tv-exhibit-daddy-yankee-morat-1236466183/|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=Garcia|first=Thania|date=July 21, 2025|access-date=August 5, 2025|archive-date=July 25, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250725013940/https://variety.com/2025/music/news/hybe-latin-america-reality-tv-exhibit-daddy-yankee-morat-1236466183/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In June 2024, Exile Music was rebranded as Zarpazo and relocated to Miami, while its podcast service was renamed Ajá Podcasts.<ref>{{Cite magazine|title=Detrás de la expansión latina de HYBE con Jonghyun 'JH' Kah, CEO de HYBE América Latina|url=https://www.billboard.com/espanol/negocios/hybe-se-expande-a-america-latina-jonghyun-jh-kah-ceo-entrevista-1235718979/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|language=es-ES|last=Cobo|first=Leila|date=June 27, 2024|access-date=September 29, 2024|archive-date=June 27, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240627140125/https://www.billboard.com/espanol/negocios/hybe-se-expande-a-america-latina-jonghyun-jh-kah-ceo-entrevista-1235718979/|url-status=live}}</ref> The establishment of new label Docemil Music was also announced.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE enters Latin music market with new label DOCEMIL Music and artist signing|url=https://biz.chosun.com/en/2025/02/05/52N2A6FPC5AJ5HUQ4XR5OV2X3Y/|website=CHOSUNBIZ|last=CHOSUNBIZ|date=February 5, 2025|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915025008/https://biz.chosun.com/en/2025/02/05/52N2A6FPC5AJ5HUQ4XR5OV2X3Y/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Hybe Latin America will operate the Docemil and Zarpazo brands, with the aim of combining Hybe's K-pop development model with local strategies to target markets in Mexico and the [[Hispanic and Latino Americans|U.S. Hispanic community]].<ref>{{Cite magazine|title=HYBE Latin America Launches Reality Series to Find Next Latin Boy Band|url=https://www.billboard.com/business/business-news/hybe-latin-america-male-pop-band-reality-series-1235969928/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Cobo|first=Leila|date=May 13, 2025|access-date=August 5, 2025|archive-date=May 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250513181703/https://www.billboard.com/business/business-news/hybe-latin-america-male-pop-band-reality-series-1235969928/|url-status=live}}</ref> The division manages artists including [[Morat (band)|Morat]] and [[Daddy Yankee]] and operates a touring agency for acts such as [[Quevedo (singer)|Quevedo]] and [[Cypress Hill]].<ref name="Garcia" /><ref>{{Cite magazine|title=Morat Signs With WK Entertainment and HYBE Latin America for Global Expansion|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/morat-deal-wk-entertainment-hybe-latin-america/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Roiz|first=Jessica|date=July 14, 2025|access-date=August 5, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915025101/https://www.billboard.com/pro/morat-deal-wk-entertainment-hybe-latin-america/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Its projects include ''[[Santos Bravos]]'', a reality show to form the Latin boy band [[Santos Bravos (group)|Santos Bravos]],<ref>{{Cite magazine|title=Meet Santos Bravos: HYBE Latin America's Search for the Next Latin Pop Superstars|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/latin/santos-bravos-hybe-latin-america-next-latin-pop-group-1236016469/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Raygoza|first=Isabela|date=July 9, 2025|access-date=August 5, 2025|archive-date=July 21, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250721215501/https://www.billboard.com/music/latin/santos-bravos-hybe-latin-america-next-latin-pop-group-1236016469/|url-status=live}}</ref> and ''[[Pase a la Fama]]'', a competition in partnership with [[Telemundo]] to select members of a [[Regional Mexican]] band.<ref>{{Cite magazine|title=Telemundo, HYBE Latin America Launch Music Competition Show to Discover Next Regional Mexican Band|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/latin/telemundo-hybe-music-competition-show-regional-mexican-band-1235954248/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Raygoza|first=Isabela|date=April 24, 2025|access-date=August 5, 2025|archive-date=April 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250424191451/https://www.billboard.com/music/latin/telemundo-hybe-music-competition-show-regional-mexican-band-1235954248/|url-status=live}}</ref> Additionally, the division launched the Hybe Experience, an interactive exhibition in Mexico City.<ref>{{Cite magazine|title=HYBE Latin America Opens Interactive Santos Bravos Exhibit Allowing Fans to 'Touch and Feel Everything That Goes Into Creating a Band'|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/latin/hybe-latin-america-santos-bravos-interactive-exhibit-mexico-1236026143/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Cano|first=Natalia|date=July 21, 2025|access-date=August 5, 2025|archive-date=September 9, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250909021646/https://www.billboard.com/music/latin/hybe-latin-america-santos-bravos-interactive-exhibit-mexico-1236026143/|url-status=live}}</ref>

