===Technology===
{{Anchor|Hybe Solutions}}
The "tech-driven future growth" division is made up of specialized business units for video content, [[Intellectual property|IP]], learning, and games. Secondary and tertiary businesses are created based on the creative output of each label.<ref name="MBW Hybe presentation" /> In May 2021, Hybe Edu signed a business agreement with the International Korean Language Education Foundation (IKLEF) to develop Korean-language textbooks for distribution to overseas elementary and secondary schools through the Ministry of Education beginning in 2022. Various other online and offline content will also be created using BTS IP in response to an increasing demand for Korean-language education in foreign countries.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:하이브 에듀, 해외 초·중등학교 공교육용 한국어 교재 개발 착수|trans-title=Hybe Edu launches development of Korean language textbooks for public education in overseas elementary and secondary schools|url=http://isplus.live.joins.com/news/article/article.asp?total_id=24060517|work=[[Ilgan Sports|Daily Sports]]|language=ko|last=Kim|first=Yeon-ji|date=May 18, 2021|access-date=May 18, 2021|archive-date=May 18, 2021|archive-url=https://archive.today/20210518064354/http://isplus.live.joins.com/news/article/article.asp?total_id=24060517|url-status=live}}</ref> In July 2021, it was announced that Hybe Solutions subsidiaries Hybe 360 and Hybe IP had been merged into Hybe.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:합병등 종료보고서|trans-title=Merger, etc. Closing Report|url=https://dart.fss.or.kr/dsaf001/main.do?rcpNo=20210702000447|publisher=Hybe Corporation|language=ko|date=July 2, 2021|access-date=September 4, 2021|archive-date=September 4, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210904130854/https://dart.fss.or.kr/dsaf001/main.do?rcpNo=20210702000447|url-status=live}}</ref> On June 22, 2022, Cake Corporation announced that Hybe Edu had been bought by them on June 1, but would continue to carry out the activities of the latter.<ref>{{Cite AV media|script-title=ko:HYBE EDU의 새 이름, Cake X|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-8mAO51pny8|via=[[YouTube]]|last=Cake X|date=August 29, 2022|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=August 29, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220829070801/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-8mAO51pny8|url-status=live}}</ref> On July 1, 2025, Hybe IM was renamed to Drimage.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE IM rebrands as Drimage, launching new interactive media era in gaming|url=https://biz.chosun.com/en/2025/07/01/ZEDBLYHR2BGLLJHXVQRNAAZ57Q/|website=CHOSUNBIZ|last=CHOSUNBIZ|date=July 1, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915024052/https://biz.chosun.com/en/2025/07/01/ZEDBLYHR2BGLLJHXVQRNAAZ57Q/|url-status=live}}</ref>

* Drimage (formerly Superb and Hybe IM)
* Hybe NEB
* Supertone (to-be dissolved)

==Disputes and legal actions==
===Dispute with Min Hee-jin===
On April 22, 2024, Hybe requested for [[Min Hee-jin]], the then-CEO of their sub-label ADOR, to step down from her position following an [[audit]] of the label amidst accusations of Min attempting to make Ador independent.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE launches audit into Ador's management amid spin-off allegations|url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/www/art/2024/04/398_373235.html|website=[[The Korea Times]]|last=Ko|first=Dong-hwan|date=April 22, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-date=April 22, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240422140556/https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/www/art/2024/04/398_373235.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:"하이브 비공개 문건 빼와"...민희진, 부정행위 포착 감사|trans-title="Take Hybe's private documents"... Min Hee-jin audited to uncover misconduct|url=https://www.dispatch.co.kr/2289124|website=[[Dispatch (South Korea)|Dispatch]]|language=ko|last=Kim|first=Ji-ho|date=April 22, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-date=April 22, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240422222610/https://www.dispatch.co.kr/2289124|url-status=live}}</ref> Min released a statement dismissing those claims and also accused Hybe of overlooking the similarities between [[NewJeans]] and [[Illit]], a girl group that debuted in March 2024 under Hybe's sub-label Belift Lab. In her statement, she accused Hybe and Belift of refusing to acknowledge the claims of [[Illit]] plagiarizing [[NewJeans]]' image from music to style, with the former's debut causing confusion amongst fans online.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Copycats? NewJeans' boss reportedly hits fellow HYBE group ILLIT|url=https://www.abs-cbn.com/entertainment/2024/4/22/copycats-newjeans-boss-reportedly-hits-fellow-hybe-group-illit-2010|website=ABS-CBN News|publisher=[[ABS-CBN Corporation]]|last=Bernardo|first=Jaehwa|date=April 22, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-date=April 26, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240426004758/https://news.abs-cbn.com/entertainment/2024/4/22/copycats-newjeans-boss-reportedly-hits-fellow-hybe-group-illit-2010|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=ADOR CEO slams HYBE group ILLIT as 'NewJeans copycat'|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-22/business/industry/ADOR-CEO-calls-HYBE-group-ILLIT-a-NewJeans-copycat/2031033|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last=Lee|first=Jae-lim|date=April 22, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425164251/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-22/business/industry/ADOR-CEO-calls-HYBE-group-ILLIT-a-NewJeans-copycat/2031033|url-status=live}}</ref> The value of Hybe's shares fell by 8.03% following the news.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:[특징주] 하이브, 뉴진스 만든 민희진 감사 착수 소식에 급락|trans-title=[Spotlight] Hybe plunges following news that NewJeans' creator, Min Hee-jin, is being audited|url=https://biz.chosun.com/stock/stock_general/2024/04/22/MPXNAC5F7FHRHLNSYZRFYPIZ44/|website=[[ChosunBiz]]|publisher=[[The Chosun Ilbo]]|language=ko|last=Kwon|first=O-eun|date=April 22, 2024|access-date=April 22, 2024|archive-date=April 22, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240422142258/https://biz.chosun.com/stock/stock_general/2024/04/22/MPXNAC5F7FHRHLNSYZRFYPIZ44/|url-status=live}}</ref> In response, Hybe submitted evidence to judicial authorities to refute the claims of plagiarism. A later court case dismissed the plagiarism claims.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:法 결정문 보니, "아일릿 표절로 보기 어려워, '뉴 버리고'도 마찬가지" [이슈&톡]|url=https://www.tvdaily.co.kr/read.php3?aid=17425390551745331010&gopc=1|website=m.tvdaily.co.kr|language=ko|date=March 21, 2025|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915031745/https://www.tvdaily.co.kr/read.php3?aid=17425390551745331010&gopc=1|url-status=live}}</ref>

Hybe officially reported Min Hee-jin to the police for "breach of trust" on April 25 following evidence retrieved from the audit that she is attempting to gain management of the label. Hybe later released text messages between Min and ADOR's vice president listing a series of methods to take control of the label. Hybe has also stated that they plan to meet with the legal representatives of NewJeans' members to discuss providing them with psychological and emotional care to support them for a successful return in the future.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE to report ADOR CEO Min Hee-jin to police|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-25/business/industry/HYBE-to-report-ADOR-CEO-Min-Heejin-/2033359|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last=Yoon|first=So-yeon|date=April 25, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425114446/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-25/business/industry/HYBE-to-report-ADOR-CEO-Min-Heejin-/2033359|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:하이브, 민희진 오늘 고발..."대화록 물증 입수했다" [공식]|trans-title=Today Hybe accuses Min Hee-jin...'We have obtained evidence of conversation transcripts' [Official]|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/468/0001054347|via=[[Naver]]|website=[[Sports Seoul]]|language=ko|last=Kim|first=Hyun-deok|date=April 25, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425053548/https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/468/0001054347|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":4">{{Cite web|title=HYBE pushed NewJeans aside for Le Sserafim, says Min Hee-jin|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-25/business/industry/HYBE-pushed-NewJeans-aside-for-Le-Sserafim-says-Min-Heejin/2033888|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last1=Yoon|first1=So-yeon|last2=Cho|first2=Yong-jun|date=April 25, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425114447/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-25/business/industry/HYBE-pushed-NewJeans-aside-for-Le-Sserafim-says-Min-Heejin/2033888|url-status=live}}</ref> It was also announced that NewJeans, who are set to release a new single in May, will carry out activities as planned.<ref>{{Cite web|title=EXCLUSIVE: NewJeans comeback will proceed as planned, despite HYBE-ADOR drama|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-23/business/industry/EXCLUSIVE-NewJeans-comeback-will-proceed-as-planned-despite-HYBEADOR-drama/2031986|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last=Lee|first=Jae-lim|date=April 23, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425114450/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-23/business/industry/EXCLUSIVE-NewJeans-comeback-will-proceed-as-planned-despite-HYBEADOR-drama/2031986|url-status=live}}</ref>

On April 25, seven hours after the report was filed, Min held an emergency press conference to deny the accusations against her. During the conference, she shared text messages exchanged between her, Bang Si-hyuk, and Hybe's former CEO Jiwon Park, some of which included Bang mentioning groups outside of Hybe. She accused Hybe of fabricating her words and revealed that she had filed an internal report in the past because the company failed to address her concerns over their treatment of NewJeans and her as a producer, however, this was ignored by the management.<ref name=":5">{{Cite web|title=As it happened — ADOR CEO Min Hee-jin press conference|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-25/entertainment/kpop/LIVE-UPDATES--ADOR-CEO-Min-Heejin-press-conference/2033613|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last1=Yoon|first1=So-yeon|last2=Cho|first2=Yong-jun|date=April 25, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425160100/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-04-25/entertainment/kpop/LIVE-UPDATES--ADOR-CEO-Min-Heejin-press-conference/2033613|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":4" /><ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:민희진 대표, 뉴진스 언급하며 눈물 "혜인이 20분동안 엉엉 울어"|trans-title=Min Hee-jin tears up at the mention of NewJeans 'Hye-in cried for 20 minutes'|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/241/0003346630|via=[[Naver]]|website=[[Ilgan Sports]]|language=ko|last=Park|first=Se-yeon|date=April 25, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 26, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240426005228/https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/241/0003346630|url-status=live}}</ref> Issues regarding Hybe's leadership also came to light as Min accused Bang of trying to control all of Hybe's labels and removing their uniqueness. Min also stated that she's willing to talk to either Bang or Park but they never agreed.<ref name=":5" /><ref name=":4" />

Hybe requested for Ador to organize a board meeting on April 30. If the board members refuse to attend, then a request would be filed in court to open a shareholders' meeting for the label. The company also refuted all of Min's claims, additionally stating that she should respond to the audit and promptly step down from her position.<ref name=":4" /><ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:하이브 "민희진 대표 기자회견, 답변할 가치 없어...정보자산 반납·신속히 감사에 응해달라"|trans-title=Hybe 'Min Hee-jin's press conference is not worth answering... Return information assets - please respond to the audit as soon as possible'|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/396/0000674627|via=[[Naver]]|website=Sports World|language=ko|last=Hyun|first=Jeong-min|date=April 25, 2024|access-date=April 25, 2024|archive-date=April 25, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425232025/https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/396/0000674627|url-status=live}}</ref> Following a court case held on May 30, Min's injunction to stop Hybe from exercising their voting rights to dismiss her was accepted by the court. Meanwhile, the ruling noted that Min had sought to weaken Hybe's control over ADOR by attempting to remove NewJeans from Hybe's influence or by pressuring Hybe to sell its stake in ADOR, thereby enabling herself to take independent control of the label<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:하이브, 법원 판결 '존중'...반격 카드는|url=https://www.thebell.co.kr/free/content/ArticleView.asp?key=202405301922026560109252|website=더벨뉴스|language=ko|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915031921/https://www.thebell.co.kr/free/content/ArticleView.asp?key=202405301922026560109252|url-status=live}}</ref> In respect of the court's decision, Hybe did not exercise its voting rights.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:'의결권 행사금지' 하이브 "법원 판단 존중...법 테두리 안에서 민희진 후속 절차"|url=https://www.news1.kr/life-culture/general-cultural/5432798|website=뉴스1|language=ko|date=May 30, 2024|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=July 13, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240713223410/https://www.news1.kr/life-culture/general-cultural/5432798|url-status=live}}</ref> If Hybe were to violate this and fire her, they would have to pay a compensation of {{KRWConvert|20|b|lk=on}}.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:[속보] 법원 "하이브, 민희진 의결권행사금지 가처분신청 인용..해임시 200억 배상 결정"|trans-title=[Breaking] Court "Hybe granted preliminary injunction to prohibit Min Hee-jin from exercising voting rights and will pay 20 billion won in case of dismissal"|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/241/0003354124|via=[[Naver]]|website=[[Ilgan Sports]]|language=ko|last=Jang|first=Joo-yeon|date=May 30, 2024|access-date=May 30, 2024|archive-date=May 30, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240530134924/https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/241/0003354124|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:법원 "하이브, 민희진 해임안 의결권 행사 안돼" 가처분 인용...어도어 대표직 유지|trans-title=Court grants preliminary injunction against Hybe's vote to remove Min Hee-jin... Ador CEO to remain in charge|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/396/0000678041|via=[[Naver]]|website=Sports World|language=ko|last=Ji|first=Dong-hyun|date=May 30, 2024|access-date=May 30, 2024|archive-date=May 30, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240530104019/https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/396/0000678041|url-status=live}}</ref>

In July 2024, Min filed police complaints against five Hybe executives on charges of defamation and business obstruction. The police ultimately dismissed the case.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE to immediately appeal decision to clear Min Hee-jin of breach of trust charges|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-07-15/national/socialAffairs/HYBE-to-immediately-appeal-decision-to-clear-Min-Heejin-of-breach-of-trust-charges/2353086|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|date=July 15, 2025|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=August 27, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250827085644/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-07-15/national/socialAffairs/HYBE-to-immediately-appeal-decision-to-clear-Min-Heejin-of-breach-of-trust-charges/2353086|url-status=live}}</ref>

On November 20, 2024, Min resigned from all her positions (including the board internal director) at both ADOR and Hybe.<ref>{{cite news|title=Ex-Ador CEO Min Hee-jin resigns from board, leaves K-pop label|url=https://m.koreatimes.co.kr/pages/article.asp?newsIdx=386728|work=[[The Korea Times]]|date=November 20, 2024|archive-date=November 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241121015310/https://m.koreatimes.co.kr/pages/article.asp?newsIdx=386728|url-status=live}}</ref>

On January 9, 2025, Chairman Park Jung-kyu of the tech company Davolink alleged in an interview that Min had made efforts to "poach" NewJeans. He also mentioned that there had been previous discussions between him and Min regarding potential investment and the possibility of NewJeans leaving Ador to sign exclusive contracts with another company.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Former Ador CEO accused of trying to poach NewJeans|url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/www/art/2025/01/398_390086.html|website=[[The Korea Times]]|date=January 9, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915032223/https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/entertainment/k-pop/20250109/former-ador-ceo-accused-of-trying-to-poach-newjeans|url-status=live}}</ref>

In early 2025, Min Hee-jin continued to face scrutiny over allegations of workplace misconduct and breach of trust. In January, the Ministry of Employment and Labor dismissed initial complaints of workplace harassment against her.<ref name="KoreaTimes2025-01">{{cite news|title=Ministry clears Min Hee-jin of harassment allegations|url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/www/nation/2025/01/113_366200.html|work=[[The Korea Times]]|date=January 12, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915032419/https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/opinion/20240107/frosty-fables-seouls-delayed-snowfall-and-our-climates-future|url-status=live}}</ref> However, in March, the Seoul Regional Employment and Labor Office issued an administrative fine against Min, determining that certain actions met the threshold for workplace harassment under South Korean labor law. Min appealed the decision.<ref name="JoongAng2025-03">{{cite news|title=Labor office fines Min Hee-jin over workplace harassment|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-03-18/national/socialAffairs/Labor-office-fines-Min-Hee-jin-over-harassment-claims/2345987|work=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|date=March 18, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=August 31, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250831104307/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-03-18/national/socialAffairs/Labor-office-fines-Min-Hee-jin-over-harassment-claims/2345987|url-status=live}}</ref>

In June, new developments emerged during ongoing court proceedings between Hybe and Min. Evidence presented in court included claims that Min had a hand in crafting emails that were publicly released by the families of NewJeans (then known as NJZ), raising questions about her role in shaping public narratives.<ref name="TOI2025-06">{{cite news|title=Did Min Hee Jin help write NJZ family emails? Court hears new evidence|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/k-pop/music/news/did-min-hee-jin-have-a-hand-in-creating-mail-for-njzs-family-emails-the-latest-court-hearing-reveals-new-evidence-against-former-ador-ceo/articleshow/121827136.cms|work=The Times of India|date=June 24, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=August 18, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250818125941/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/k-pop/music/news/did-min-hee-jin-have-a-hand-in-creating-mail-for-njzs-family-emails-the-latest-court-hearing-reveals-new-evidence-against-former-ador-ceo/articleshow/121827136.cms|url-status=live}}</ref>

A major legal decision occurred on July 15, when the Seoul Yongsan Police Station cleared Min of all breach of trust allegations that had been filed by Hybe in April 2024. Authorities concluded there was insufficient evidence to pursue criminal charges.<ref name="KoreaTimes2025-07">{{cite news|title=Former ADOR chief Min Hee-jin cleared of breach of trust charges|url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/law-crime/20250715/former-ador-chief-min-hee-jin-cleared-of-breach-of-trust-charges|work=[[The Korea Times]]|date=July 15, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=August 1, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250801112056/https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/law-crime/20250715/former-ador-chief-min-hee-jin-cleared-of-breach-of-trust-charges|url-status=live}}</ref>

Following the decision, Hybe announced its intent to appeal, stating that it had uncovered new evidence and legal grounds to challenge the police's conclusion.<ref name="MBW2025-07">{{cite web|title=HYBE to appeal decision clearing Min Hee-jin of breach of trust|url=https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/hybe-says-it-will-appeal-police-decision-not-to-charge-ador-ex-ceo-min-hee-jin-in-breach-of-trust-case/|website=Music Business Worldwide|date=July 16, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=August 11, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250811183208/https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/hybe-says-it-will-appeal-police-decision-not-to-charge-ador-ex-ceo-min-hee-jin-in-breach-of-trust-case/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Reuters">{{cite web|title=South Korea financial regulator refers HYBE K-pop agency chair Bang for investigation, Yonhap says|url=https://www.reuters.com/markets/asia/south-korea-financial-regulator-refers-hybe-chair-bang-investigation-yonhap-says-2025-07-16/|website=Reuters|date=July 16, 2025|access-date=August 12, 2025|archive-date=July 19, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250719030116/https://www.reuters.com/markets/asia/south-korea-financial-regulator-refers-hybe-chair-bang-investigation-yonhap-says-2025-07-16/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On February 12, 2026, it was reported that the court ruled in favor of Min in both her lawsuit seeking payment for shares under a put option agreement and Hybe's lawsuit seeking confirmation that the shareholder agreement was terminated. After the validity of Min's put option right is finalized, Hybe will have to pay Min ₩25.5 billion (US$17.7 million).<ref>{{cite news|title=In $17M ruling, Min Hee-jin appears to gain momentum in other suits, lose face with NewJeans fans|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2026-02-12/national/socialAffairs/In-17M-ruling-Min-Heejin-appears-to-gain-momentum-in-other-suits-lose-face-with-NewJeans-fans/2523006|work=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last=Yoon|first=So-yeon|date=February 12, 2026|access-date=February 12, 2026}}</ref>

===Employee insider trading===
In June 2024, South Korean prosecutors charged three employees of subsidiaries affiliated with Hybe with insider trading. The individuals were accused of selling company shares shortly before the public announcement on June 14, 2022, that members of the K-pop group BTS would be taking a hiatus. Prosecutors stated that the employees had access to non-public information about the announcement, which enabled them to sell their shares in advance and avoid financial losses estimated between US$24,000 and US$108,000,<ref>{{cite news|title=K-pop agents charged with insider trading over BTS|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1vd7y5rnnwo|work=[[BBC]]|last=da Silva|first=João|date=June 28, 2024|access-date=July 3, 2024|archive-date=July 3, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240703004152/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1vd7y5rnnwo|url-status=live}}</ref> which the three denied during their first hearing at trial.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Hybe staff deny insider trading in first trial hearing|url=https://www.koreaherald.com/article/3829897|website=[[The Korea Herald]]|last=Sung-mi|first=Ahn|date=October 22, 2024|access-date=August 14, 2025|archive-date=January 22, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122171617/https://www.koreaherald.com/article/3829897|url-status=live}}</ref>

On July 22, 2025, the three individuals—who were no longer employed at Hybe at the time of sentencing—received suspended prison sentences ranging from six months to two years. In addition to the suspended terms, the court imposed financial penalties ranging from approximately {{KRWConvert|51|m}} to {{KRWConvert|231|m}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Update (2): Three former HYBE employees receive sentences for insider trading on BTS' military enlistment (report)|url=https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/three-employees-receive-prison-sentence-for-insider-trading-on-bts-military-enlistment-report/|website=Music Business Worldwide|last=Dalugdug|first=Mandy|date=July 24, 2025|access-date=July 30, 2025|archive-date=July 26, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250726221845/https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/three-employees-receive-prison-sentence-for-insider-trading-on-bts-military-enlistment-report/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE employees sentenced to prison for insider trading on BTS's military service|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-07-22/business/finance/HYBE-employee-sentenced-to-prison-for-insider-trading-on-BTSs-military-service/2358636|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|date=July 22, 2025|access-date=July 30, 2025|archive-date=July 22, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722113030/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-07-22/business/finance/HYBE-employee-sentenced-to-prison-for-insider-trading-on-BTSs-military-service/2358636|url-status=live}}</ref>

Separately, on May 29, prosecutors from the Seoul Southern District Prosecutors Office raided the headquarters of Hybe as part of an investigation into allegations of fraudulent trading. A former Hybe executive was accused of earning approximately {{KRWConvert|240|m}} in profits through insider trading by purchasing shares in [[YG Plus]] after obtaining non-public information about Hybe's planned investment in the company.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Prosecutors search K-pop powerhouse Hybe over allegations of fraudulent trading|url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/20250529/prosecutors-search-k-pop-powerhouse-hybe-over-allegations-of-fraudulent-trading|website=[[The Korea Times]]|date=May 29, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915032524/https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/20250529/prosecutors-search-k-pop-powerhouse-hybe-over-allegations-of-fraudulent-trading|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Prosecutors raid K-pop agency HYBE over suspected insider trading|url=https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20250529011400320|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|date=May 29, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915032616/https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20250529011400320|url-status=live}}</ref> Hybe stated that it was fully cooperating with authorities and reiterated its commitment to legal compliance and transparency.<ref>{{Cite web|title=HYBE Cooperating With Authorities Amid Insider Trading Allegations|url=https://au.variety.com/2025/music/news/hybe-cooperating-with-authorities-allegations-insider-trading-23170/|website=Variety Australia|date=May 29, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=September 15, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250915032658/https://au.variety.com/2025/music/news/hybe-cooperating-with-authorities-allegations-insider-trading-23170/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Leaked audit documents===
On October 24, 2024, Hybe came under public scrutiny during a National Assembly audit, when Representative Min Hyung-bae of the Democratic Party questioned Hybe's Chief Operating Officer, Taeho Kim, about the company's internal practices. During the session, Min disclosed the existence of an internal company document titled Weekly Music Industry Report—a collection reportedly totaling approximately 18,000 pages. The report allegedly contained derogatory remarks, unverified rumors, and harsh commentary about various K-pop idols. Portions of the document were later leaked online, prompting widespread criticism.

In response, on October 29, Hybe CEO Jason Jaesang Lee issued a public apology. He described the report as a compilation of external opinions and reactions related to K-pop trends, intended for internal analysis by a limited number of executives. Lee acknowledged that the content was "highly inappropriate and unacceptable" and expressed regret over the harm caused. He stated that Hybe was in the process of directly contacting affected agencies to offer apologies, and he also personally apologized to the company's artists who had been criticized in the leaked material.<ref>{{cite magazine|title=HYBE CEO Lee Jae-Sang Apologizes Over Leaked Company Document Critical of K-Pop Artists & More|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/hybe-ceo-apologizes-leaked-document-criticizing-k-pop-stars/|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Benjamin|first=Jeff|date=October 29, 2024|access-date=November 9, 2024|archive-date=November 9, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241109154056/https://www.billboard.com/pro/hybe-ceo-apologizes-leaked-document-criticizing-k-pop-stars/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=HYBE Apologizes for Leaked 'Music Industry Report' as Court Denies Min Heejin's ADOR CEO Request|url=https://www.teenvogue.com/story/hybe-apologizes-for-leaked-music-industry-report-as-court-denies-min-heejins-ador-ceo-request|work=[[Teen Vogue]]|last=Delgado|first=Sara|date=October 30, 2024|access-date=November 9, 2024|archive-date=November 9, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241109154112/https://www.teenvogue.com/story/hybe-apologizes-for-leaked-music-industry-report-as-court-denies-min-heejins-ador-ceo-request|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=HYBE CEO apologizes for controversial internal document|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-10-29/entertainment/kpop/HYBE-CEO-apologizes-for-controversial-internal-document/2165857|work=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|last=Yoon|first=Seung-jin|date=October 29, 2024|access-date=November 9, 2024|archive-date=November 9, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241109154126/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2024-10-29/entertainment/kpop/HYBE-CEO-apologizes-for-controversial-internal-document/2165857|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Tax investigation===
On July 29, 2025, the National Tax Service (NTS) of South Korea conducted a search and seizure operation at Hybe's headquarters in Yongsan, Seoul. This action was part of a broader investigation by the NTS's 4th Investigation Bureau into alleged tax evasion and irregular financial activities involving 27 companies. Hybe was among the businesses suspected of engaging in unfair stock practices and underreporting tax liabilities.<ref name="TI - JoonAng">{{Cite web|title=HYBE under investigation for stock manipulation and tax evasion|url=https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-07-29/national/socialAffairs/HYBE-under-investigation-for-stock-manipulation-and-tax-evasion/2363973|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|date=July 29, 2025|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=July 29, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250729152422/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/2025-07-29/national/socialAffairs/HYBE-under-investigation-for-stock-manipulation-and-tax-evasion/2363973|url-status=live}}</ref>

The probe specifically focused on Hybe's 2020 initial public offering (IPO) and transactions that preceded it. Authorities are investigating claims that Hybe and its executives, including founder and chairman Bang Si-hyuk, misled investors in 2019 by publicly stating that there were no plans for a stock market listing, while secretly preparing for an IPO. The company later proceeded with the listing, and Bang is alleged to have gained hundreds of billions of won in profits through a special purpose vehicle (SPV) that acquired shares on his behalf. Prosecutors believe Bang may have received as much as 30% of the proceeds from this SPV-linked transaction.<ref name="TI - JoonAng" />

This marked the first tax raid on Hybe since June 2022, when a routine audit by the Seoul Regional Tax Office led to the imposition of a "a multi-billion-won penalty."<ref>{{Cite web|title=South Korean tax authorities open probe into HYBE amid stock manipulation claims against Chairman Bang Si-hyuk|url=https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/south-korean-tax-authorities-open-probe-into-hybe-amid-stock-manipulation-claims-against-chairman-bang-si-hyuk/|website=Music Business Worldwide|last=Dalugdug|first=Mandy|date=July 30, 2025|access-date=August 15, 2025|archive-date=August 11, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250811165414/https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/south-korean-tax-authorities-open-probe-into-hybe-amid-stock-manipulation-claims-against-chairman-bang-si-hyuk/|url-status=live}}</ref> The 2025 raid, however, signaled a significant escalation, as it followed two previous legal actions within the same month: one involving insider trading by Hybe executives and another centered on IPO-related fraud allegations relating to the founder, Bang Si-hyuk. Combined, these investigations reflect mounting legal and regulatory pressure on the entertainment conglomerate.<ref name="TI - JoonAng" />

On April 21, 2026, South Korean police sought an arrest warrant for Hybe founder and chairperson Bang Si-hyuk over alleged violations of capital market laws related to Hybe's initial public offering, accusing him of misleading early investors and receiving profits through a related private equity fund. <ref>{{Cite web|title=South Korean police seek to arrest K-pop mogul behind BTS|url=https://apnews.com/article/south-korea-bang-hybe-arrest-bts-00e181bfbe471c541118d67f7ccad7bd|website=AP News|last=Tong-Hyung|first=Kim|date=April 22, 2026|access-date=April 25, 2026}}</ref>

